path.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T02:56:27-07:00","id":1465748,"title":"","content":"yesssss...very enjoyable, can feel the hype.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T10:01:43-07:00","id":1466666,"title":"","content":"Dixie Cochran becomes Anima world 'youtuber' that talks news about <b>Terra Surge</b> MMO of this world...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u78wo7enBlI\" data-code=\"u78wo7enBlI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/u78wo7enBlI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T20:00:41-08:00","id":1467229,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Trinity </span>Anima</b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> Kickstarter is starting on November 18th! Here's how the creators sum up what he is! (Sounds like more digestible postpunk, even <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</span><br /> <br /> <b>What is Trinity Continuum: Anima?</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">* <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b>A brand-new Trinity Continuum game.</b> </span>Unlike TC: \u00c6on, TC: Aberrant, and TC: Adventure!, this isn\u2019t the second edition of a previously made game. This is a completely new setting in the year 2084, sitting between TC: \u00c6on and TC: Aberrant.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">* <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b>A new take on cyberpunk.</b> </span>Unlike a hundred gritty, worn-down cyberpunk dystopias, the city of Cascade is shiny and new. Characters will still fight a fascist government and unethical corporations, but they do so in a gleaming city full of potential and hope.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">* <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b>A video game in an RPG.</b> </span>This isn\u2019t just a tabletop adaptation of a popular video game; this is a new system that allows the characters of TC: Anima to themselves play in a fully immersive MMO. The rules are designed to make the experience feel like playing in a video game.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">* <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b>A modern take on cyberware.</b> </span>No loss of \u201chumanity\u201d or \u201cessence\u201d happens in TC: Anima. Nearly every character has cyberware, either as a brain implant or as assistive devices after a devastating war. Using cyberware doesn\u2019t make you less of a person, but it does open new dramatic possibilities.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">* <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b>A mystery you can dig into right away.</b> </span>Streamers of the popular video game Terra Surge are disappearing. Why? That question is something that can draw the player characters in immediately, or Storyguides can focus on other parts of the setting to create their own conflicts and intrigues.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/photo/?fbid=10217199718059915&amp;set=gm.10158759086547371&amp;__cft__&#91;0]=AZW9miXFDMDAmm2-vfMjS0BBt_VgLYVSnHkX83aluvGR8Tts-ZEw_4Xb2vKD6ueuQSQ9zNrNiIg-aqtSkhw92-9kdcuq7H83GrdHRUHIfz5t4kGKLiWVjs7niWvBh9qwG786jjzYmcP0Q4ACLAZTwzJEeiyhpfJKY4zvSiReyKruvFwWtAtHLROLCCLZnHjy0ko&amp;__tn__=EH-R\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://scontent-waw1-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t1.6435-9/254957377_10217199718099916_6616286055519887971_n.jpg?_nc_cat=109&amp;ccb=1-5&amp;_nc_sid=825194&amp;_nc_ohc=1YOBf0cEANkAX8Ldags&amp;_nc_ht=scontent-waw1-1.xx&amp;oh=6727fe05d1e00e37aa36f2d714e40fa4&amp;oe=61B10530\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></span></span></span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T00:13:25-08:00","id":1467239,"title":"","content":"Anima sounds so cool! Can't wait to see what powers Anima PCs can have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T00:23:43-08:00","id":1467240,"title":"","content":"Huh. Is this going to be like Orpheus in the old world of darkness? Like a game that is kind of like a miniseries with a really focused story line? I mean according to the timeline in 2086 the Shanghai Accords probably results in Terra Surge and the Glass implant getting outlawed. I'm guessing the player characters of Anima end up taking the whole thing down?<br /> <br /> Seems like an interesting idea but fairly limited in scope. Not really the galaxy spanning adventure you can take part in Aeon.<br /> <br /> Is there going to be alternate future possibilities presented in the book that discuss what might result if brain implants and immersive mmo's like presented in the Anima setting remain common place and accessible to people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T01:13:16-08:00","id":1467244,"title":"","content":"Anima Actual Play has something like <b><i>A</i></b><i><b><b><i>e</i></b>on Covenant</b></i> - I suspect it's foundation for proper Aeon in<b> TC Aeon</b> setting, made up from Allegiances after Aberrant? Can someone explain this to me?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ahL_PqMtDvE\" data-code=\"ahL_PqMtDvE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ahL_PqMtDvE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> First info are in 30 seconds of video, so just play it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-09-2021, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T01:32:22-08:00","id":1467245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1467240#post1467240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there going to be alternate future possibilities presented in the book that discuss what might result if brain implants and immersive mmo's like presented in the Anima setting remain common place and accessible to people?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every single era book about Trinity can fork off on it's own possible future.<br /> <br /> If you want your game to never end and keep playing Anima forever even into the far future, you can.<br /> <br /> The timeline in any book is a guideline but not immutable and untouchable.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T03:16:07-08:00","id":1467247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMrMultiverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1467239#post1467239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anima sounds so cool! Can't wait to see what powers Anima PCs can have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cybernetics, including the Glass that allows for direct brain interface with the MMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T04:26:58-08:00","id":1467249,"title":"","content":"The Anima setting is limited to Cascades an the FSA or we will have an ambientation that includes all the world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25829-vjornin","name":"Vjornin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T12:17:40-08:00","id":1467277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1467245#post1467245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every single era book about Trinity can fork off on it's own possible future.<br /> <br /> If you want your game to never end and keep playing Anima forever even into the far future, you can.<br /> <br /> The timeline in any book is a guideline but not immutable and untouchable.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I know that is an explicit part of the setting this time around, what with the whole continuum concept. I was asking if they actually had some scenario examples for different possible futures rather then the Trinity base timeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T13:10:14-08:00","id":1467285,"title":"","content":"While brain interactive implants are forbidden later in the timeline, there are versions that are not implants, regular gloves and glasses, and possibly a suit (like Player One Read stuff).<br /> <br /> Also, as many cyberpunk, it becoming illegal also brings some story to the table: will you remove it? Are Aberrants going through your brain thanks to the implant? It has advantages and disadvantages. If the idea is to follow the timeline to Aeon, it would be an interesting game.<br /> <br /> Now, on the other question, Anima is largely focused in Cascade and the virtual reality, but I think they will talk about the rest of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T20:40:11-08:00","id":1467322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1467240#post1467240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Is this going to be like Orpheus in the old world of darkness? Like a game that is kind of like a miniseries with a really focused story line?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like every TC game line, we'll have as many supplements as we think we can fund and get away with. Other game lines thus far had 20+ years of support from an existing fanbase, so they were comparatively an easy sell. Anima is new, so the degree of support will depend on how well it performs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean according to the timeline in 2086 the Shanghai Accords probably results in Terra Surge and the Glass implant getting outlawed. I'm guessing the player characters of Anima end up taking the whole thing down? </div> </div> </div>I have previously strongly suggested that the events of Anima are what leads to the Shanghai Accords. How that plays out (or not) is up to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seems like an interesting idea but fairly limited in scope. Not really the galaxy spanning adventure you can take part in Aeon. </div> </div> </div>Well, we already have a galaxy-spanning game, which is \u00c6on. If that's what you want, it's already there. The whole point of having different genres for each game line in the Continuum is that we can do different things with them. A lot of cyberpunk games and settings are focused on the event of a single city. That doesn't mean that there aren't endless stories to tell. Blade Runner's LA, Altered Carbon's Bay City, Remember Me's Neo-Paris, the City of Mirror's Edge, Ghost in the Shell's Niihama.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there going to be alternate future possibilities presented in the book that discuss what might result if brain implants and immersive mmo's like presented in the Anima setting remain common place and accessible to people? </div> </div> </div>Alternate futures are a common element of the Setting Secrets appendix at the end of each Trinity Continuum rulebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":4,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","user":"IanWatson","date":". 11-09-2021, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T23:56:31-08:00","id":1467330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1467322#post1467322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternate futures are a common element of the Setting Secrets appendix at the end of each Trinity Continuum rulebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. I really liked the setting secrets in Aeon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T01:33:06-08:00","id":1467334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1467285#post1467285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While brain interactive implants are forbidden later in the timeline, there are versions that are not implants, regular gloves and glasses, and possibly a suit (like Player One Read stuff).<br /> <br /> Also, as many cyberpunk, it becoming illegal also brings some story to the table: will you remove it? Are Aberrants going through your brain thanks to the implant? It has advantages and disadvantages. If the idea is to follow the timeline to Aeon, it would be an interesting game.</div> </div> </div> </div>My fan theory, for now, is whatever is going on with <i>Mystery of Disappearances in Terra Surge</i>, will come to ban cybernetics after <b>Anima</b> events.<b> Anima</b> PCs ARE playing through huge social change that help create next TC setting 'in line', <b>Aeon</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4\" data-vbnamecard=\"4\">IanWatson</a> <i>- '</i><i>I have previously strongly suggested that the events of Anima are what leads to the Shanghai Accords. How that plays out (or not) is up to you.'</i> - And now we have Word of the God on the subject. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-10-2021, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T06:04:13-08:00","id":1467345,"title":"","content":"Well, without a defined Metaplot, all we will have is the Secrets chapter. Let\u2019s see next month (when we get there)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T00:31:31-08:00","id":1468950,"title":"","content":"So no real conversation about the casual revelations in Preview 2? Specifically as to the CEO of OP-Tec. Avoiding spoilers so as to encourage people to pledge and see for themselves, that info about them makes me reassess allot of the information in Aeon and try to figure how it could be seen in a new light.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca","name":"DarrenDalca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27184_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T01:04:57-08:00","id":1468952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarrenDalca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1468950#post1468950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So no real conversation about the casual revelations in Preview 2? Specifically as to the CEO of OP-Tec. Avoiding spoilers so as to encourage people to pledge and see for themselves, that info about them makes me reassess allot of the information in Aeon and try to figure how it could be seen in a new light.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it is not in the secrets chapter, I imagine what is\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T08:47:49-08:00","id":1468987,"title":"","content":"I think I\u2019m going to tweak the Aeon Covenant at my table. The Aeon Society is defunct after the Aberrant War, but the Covenant is a lose information sharing network between several separate organizations that owe their origins to Aeon.<br /> <br /> Task Force Proteus is an international strike force dedicated to hunting new eruptions and Aberrant cults (and keeping sub-Aberrant mutants contained in Corruption Zones). They encompass Project Ceto.<br /> <br /> Nereus Labs is researching cutting edge non-Nova paths of human evolution. They\u2019re very interested in (and nervous about) the trans human potential of Glass right now. They encompass both Pandora and Tantalus.<br /> <br /> The Maxwell Mercer Foundation is the various charitable operations. This is where Margaret is chair.<br /> <br /> And of course Project ReWrite you know<br /> <br /> I\u2019m trying to come up with of any other independent Allegiances for the era I could include in my reimagined Covenant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T03:16:54-08:00","id":1469079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarrenDalca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1468950#post1468950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So no real conversation about the casual revelations in Preview 2? Specifically as to the CEO of OP-Tec. Avoiding spoilers so as to encourage people to pledge and see for themselves, that info about them makes me reassess allot of the information in Aeon and try to figure how it could be seen in a new light.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine those revelations aren't common knowledge, even internally of OP-Tec. I believe it ties directly to certain events that directly impact \u00c6on era.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T05:21:29-08:00","id":1469087,"title":"","content":"Ok, there's something that I want to point out that has bothered me.<br /> <br /> SPOILERS<br /> <br /> So am I the only one a bit disappointed at the fate of the directive? I mean, from the largest intelligence service in the world that dealt with strange phenomena, then to the Directive to protect humanity from novas to...a minor security company focused on protecting the interests of abusive corporations...what?<br /> Here's the thing, I'm not disappointed at the what, but how they ended there. It was basically the world leaders saying, &quot;Hey, we don't need you anymore, so we're cutting funding, also we need the money to rebuild&quot; Sure, it makes sense, but isn't that a bit underwhelming?<br /> I can accept the nations of the world taking away the funding and resources as a punishment for the aberrant war, after all the Directive was created precisely to prevent something like that, and they failed, hard. That left the Directive bitter and lost, with not choice but to become mercenaries as a way to survive, and also working for the corps was a perfect way to get back at the governments that punished them.<br /> I could also accept a more heroic approach, where the Directive fought heroically to prevent and minimize the aberrant war. Even thought they failed in the end, things could have been much worse without their help. The thing is that they suffered such catastrophic losses that the world nations decided to just abandon them, since it was easier than trying to rebuild the organization. Again, they reformed into a merc company for the same reasons as before, survival and revenge.<br /> It's just a minor thing. Again, I don't mind seeing one of the major alliances fall from grace, I just expected something more from such an important organization in the history of the trinity continuum. What do you think? Would you like to share other takes?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T18:21:20-08:00","id":1469137,"title":"","content":"Probably just an example of &quot;Last Jedi&quot;ing things. Got to have old heroes fall from grace so that new heroes can take their place. That totally seems like a bummer, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T06:11:38-08:00","id":1469394,"title":"","content":"It's been a minute since I read TC Aberrant, but did the Proteus writeup seem a bit off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T07:57:11-08:00","id":1469399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1469394#post1469394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been a minute since I read TC Aberrant, but did the Proteus writeup seem a bit off?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean... it's not Aberrant or Aeon Proteus. But beyond that you're going to have to be more specific as what you mean is &quot;off&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T16:32:58-08:00","id":1469432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1469087#post1469087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, there's something that I want to point out that has bothered me.<br /> <br /> SPOILERS<br /> <br /> So am I the only one a bit disappointed at the fate of the directive? I mean, from the largest intelligence service in the world that dealt with strange phenomena, then to the Directive to protect humanity from novas to...a minor security company focused on protecting the interests of abusive corporations...what?<br /> Here's the thing, I'm not disappointed at the what, but how they ended there. It was basically the world leaders saying, &quot;Hey, we don't need you anymore, so we're cutting funding, also we need the money to rebuild&quot; Sure, it makes sense, but isn't that a bit underwhelming?<br /> I can accept the nations of the world taking away the funding and resources as a punishment for the aberrant war, after all the Directive was created precisely to prevent something like that, and they failed, hard. That left the Directive bitter and lost, with not choice but to become mercenaries as a way to survive, and also working for the corps was a perfect way to get back at the governments that punished them.<br /> I could also accept a more heroic approach, where the Directive fought heroically to prevent and minimize the aberrant war. Even thought they failed in the end, things could have been much worse without their help. The thing is that they suffered such catastrophic losses that the world nations decided to just abandon them, since it was easier than trying to rebuild the organization. Again, they reformed into a merc company for the same reasons as before, survival and revenge.<br /> It's just a minor thing. Again, I don't mind seeing one of the major alliances fall from grace, I just expected something more from such an important organization in the history of the trinity continuum. What do you think? Would you like to share other takes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not me. I think we read 9 a little differently. I certainly didn't get the impression that they were the largest (and most effective) intelligence agency in the world, since they exist alongside with other powerful agencies with similar goals such as N.O.E.R., Alert Status 1 and Project Proteus, and I suppose the CIA and NSA. With so many other organizations in the setting being hopeful do-gooders, I think that 9 also serves as an effective foil by being cynical, metamorphosing from era to era, generally serving the conservative interests of existing power structures. Honestly, I always imagine them to be like a much larger and somewhat less incompetent version of ISIS from Archer.<br /> <br /> Also, being a megacorp in a cyberpunk world is a pretty powerful position, possibly moreso than they've been in any other era. I think the manuscript said they had 300,000 employees, 200,000 of which are active security personnel equipped with and trained with weapons. That's a larger paramilitary than most national armies existing today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T23:30:59-08:00","id":1469562,"title":"","content":"Anyone else think that the Ghosts who pulled off the original hack are the precursor faction to the Ghosts of Cincinnatus from Terra Firrma?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca","name":"DarrenDalca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27184_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T05:29:30-08:00","id":1469571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarrenDalca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1469562#post1469562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else think that the Ghosts who pulled off the original hack are the precursor faction to the Ghosts of Cincinnatus from Terra Firrma?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I suspect they're a later incarnation of Les Fantomes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T14:49:18-08:00","id":1469592,"title":"","content":"In fact, p. 19 of Preview 2, under the entry for the Ghost Wolves, specifically says &quot;We are the children of Les Fant\u00f4mes and Ars\u00e8ne Lupin.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T05:44:47-08:00","id":1469643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1469592#post1469592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, p. 19 of Preview 2, under the entry for the Ghost Wolves, specifically says &quot;We are the children of Les Fant\u00f4mes and Ars\u00e8ne Lupin.&quot;<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I apparently missed that entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca","name":"DarrenDalca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27184_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T18:52:46-08:00","id":1469681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1466666#post1466666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dixie Cochran becomes Anima world 'youtuber' that talks news about <b>Terra Surge</b> MMO of this world...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u78wo7enBlI\" data-code=\"u78wo7enBlI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/u78wo7enBlI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I admit that I'm having a little trouble wrapping my head around the Terra Surge stuff. Cyberware, hacking, corporate secrets, sure. But I'm kind of bouncing off the idea of &quot;Okay, you create your character for Trinity: Anima and then, as that character, you create the character(s) that they'll be playing in Anima's version of Elder Scrolls.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T20:30:47-08:00","id":1469689,"title":"","content":"Where does it start to fall apart for you? What part is not clicking <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2318\" data-vbnamecard=\"2318\">johntfs</a> ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":786,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","user":"thedonnie","date":". 12-06-2021, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T01:18:22-08:00","id":1469706,"title":"","content":"I think it start to fall apart when they discover that Glass IS novatech and that there is a Nova behind it all, even if not in Fulgur Tech.<br /> <br /> I think Narrators have not much to do with the end, even because they are not really related to Cascade or FSA in any way other than FSA players having a different set of rules, also TerraSurge is not a Glass thing, it is a virtual reality thing, people don\u2019t need glass to play TS, and probably only a small percent of the players (most located in Cascade) use glass to play.<br /> <br /> well, we may see the real reason in a couple more weeks\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T06:21:18-08:00","id":1469724,"title":"","content":"hey i found an old short film on Youtube....it reminded me a lot of augmented reality and gamification of GLASS..take a look. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lK_cdkpazjI\" data-code=\"lK_cdkpazjI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/lK_cdkpazjI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T17:19:25-08:00","id":1469884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1469689#post1469689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does it start to fall apart for you? What part is not clicking <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2318\" data-vbnamecard=\"2318\">johntfs</a> ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fourth manuscript will likely make some of these impressions false, but basically I think the Terra Surge stuff needs to be more tightly bound to the real world. In <i>Ready Player One</i> when the protagonists completed a quest and gained treasure, he could use that treasure as real money to buy real things in the real world. Maybe something really weird happened that dumped a lot of the FSA's info into the game. Completing quests might get you access to those data havens and get you information to really take down some oppressors (and of course plenty of FSA &quot;dark knights&quot; would be in the game trying to prevent that from happening and if they take out your character in the game, they'll get your real name and address, which could screw up your life in the real world.<br /> <br /> Right now the idea of creating full secondary characters for Terra Surge seems a little silly. I'm role-playing my character playing a different character in an online RPG? At most Animas should be Edges of a sort.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T18:22:18-08:00","id":1469885,"title":"","content":"One of the biggest mysteries is that people will disappear in the MMO and then not be heard from again in the real world so being able to drop into the game to investigate is important. Also, if you watch some of the AP's that have been done show how the both are entwined in a way like you have mentioned. Although, not in a monetary way, but you can gain information in the Terra Surge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T13:43:50-08:00","id":1469955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1469885#post1469885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the biggest mysteries is that people will disappear in the MMO and then not be heard from again in the real world so being able to drop into the game to investigate is important. Also, if you watch some of the AP's that have been done show how the both are entwined in a way like you have mentioned. Although, not in a monetary way, but you can gain information in the Terra Surge.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all well and good but Terra Surge has basically been built up to be something like the Matrix. In the Matrix movies, doing things in the Matrix and having Matrix-based skills were extremely important because at least half the plot of the movies took place in the Matrix. Right now, Terra Surge doesn't live up to that. Can you maybe get some information there? Perhaps, but right now Terra Surge feels extremely optional. I still haven't really grokked why I would want to roleplayer some character who plays Trinity Skyrim instead of just, y;know, playing Skyrim.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T15:09:50-08:00","id":1469960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1469955#post1469955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's all well and good but Terra Surge has basically been built up to be something like the Matrix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps your dissatisfaction is the result of mismanaged expectations or a miscommunication somewhere -- I don't think we've ever positioned Terra Surge to be anything Matrix-like other than, for example, being able to use Glass to quickly learn a new skill.<br /> <br /> We've been pretty up-front about it being a fantasy MMO that Cascadians indulge in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T15:44:36-08:00","id":1469963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1469960#post1469960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps your dissatisfaction is the result of mismanaged expectations or a miscommunication somewhere -- I don't think we've ever positioned Terra Surge to be anything Matrix-like other than, for example, being able to use Glass to quickly learn a new skill.<br /> <br /> We've been pretty up-front about it being a fantasy MMO that Cascadians indulge in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, in any real community social activities count for a lot. Being known as a good player of a popular game would bring status. The MMO gives the PCs and alternate means of interacting with their community. Good role playing could leverage that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T12:02:36-08:00","id":1470063,"title":"","content":"This whole idea seems pretty similar to the dot hack series. The &quot;Players solving a mystery in the game&quot; thing. Anyone know if they included a &quot;people involved in the game are being put in a coma&quot; plotline in addition to the &quot;people involved with the game are disappearing&quot; plotline? Another thing about Anima seems similar to is the Earth setting of the isekai light novel &quot;Overlord&quot;. The immersive virtual reality game in that story was so popular in part because the world of the future was in such a mess. In addition to the game that people would play in the virtual reality there would also be the draw of actually getting to experience a natural, unspoiled world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T18:28:32-08:00","id":1470095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1470063#post1470063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This whole idea seems pretty similar to the dot hack series. The &quot;Players solving a mystery in the game&quot; thing. Anyone know if they included a &quot;people involved in the game are being put in a coma&quot; plotline in addition to the &quot;people involved with the game are disappearing&quot; plotline?</div> </div> </div> </div>That will be in the setting secrets manuscript previews on Tuesday<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T19:42:51-08:00","id":1470105,"title":"","content":"My concern is still that the scope of the game seems to be very narrow. Like, you are going to be running a very specific campaign. With Aeon there was definitely a big incentive for players to get involved with various big plotlines, but you didn't necessarily have to. And if you didn't get involved in the various big plots there was still a lot of cool stuff you could do. You could play asteroid miners in some out of the way star system or maybe be private investigators who are being pursued by a powerful Metacorp. Does material from Anima out so far give some ideas of the various adventures you could have that don't involve the larger metaplot? Other than experiences what exactly does playing Terra Surge offer people? Playing a game about someone playing a game is sort of interesting in a meta sense, but is there any actual stakes involved?<br /> <br /> Like my main thought is that Terra Surge involved the use of artificial intelligence in its creation so if the NPC's in the game are actual people then the player's have some more drive to care about everything. Take down that raid boss or a village of real people are going to die! Otherwise it seems like playing the game would be more like playing someone's hobby rather then something meaningful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T19:53:01-08:00","id":1470106,"title":"","content":"Well, the tech in Anima (Neural interfaces and full AI) are outlawed in 2 years from the time the game starts, it is meant to be a bit more breakneck pace. But, like all Trinity games, you can have it go on forever.<br /> It also has the fact that you can just play a whole campaign within Terra Surge all you want. There is that setting that is ripe for so much roleplay opportunities.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T07:07:07-08:00","id":1470131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1470105#post1470105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My concern is still that the scope of the game seems to be very narrow. Like, you are going to be running a very specific campaign. With Aeon there was definitely a big incentive for players to get involved with various big plotlines, but you didn't necessarily have to. And if you didn't get involved in the various big plots there was still a lot of cool stuff you could do. You could play asteroid miners in some out of the way star system or maybe be private investigators who are being pursued by a powerful Metacorp. Does material from Anima out so far give some ideas of the various adventures you could have that don't involve the larger metaplot? Other than experiences what exactly does playing Terra Surge offer people? Playing a game about someone playing a game is sort of interesting in a meta sense, but is there any actual stakes involved?<br /> <br /> Like my main thought is that Terra Surge involved the use of artificial intelligence in its creation so if the NPC's in the game are actual people then the player's have some more drive to care about everything. Take down that raid boss or a village of real people are going to die! Otherwise it seems like playing the game would be more like playing someone's hobby rather then something meaningful.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then you discover a group of Ghost Wolves debating whether they should assassinate an obviously corrupt judge IRL.<br /> <br /> Seriously. The game is doing a good job of showing that it's also incredibly useful for covert communications, and we haven't seen what the mystery that ties into the real world and what's brainwashing people by corrupting their characters yet.<br /> <br /> From there, players have the capacity to, say, influence whatever scandal blows up the AI movement so that the FSA gets the blame if (and I don't know if this is true) it turns out the weirdness is due to the FSA trying to turn the Narrators into tools of mind control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T14:59:18-08:00","id":1470477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1469960#post1469960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps your dissatisfaction is the result of mismanaged expectations or a miscommunication somewhere -- I don't think we've ever positioned Terra Surge to be anything Matrix-like other than, for example, being able to use Glass to quickly learn a new skill.<br /> <br /> We've been pretty up-front about it being a fantasy MMO that Cascadians indulge in.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the Story-telling Secrets in Nine and Ten, my issues have been handled because yeah, there's a bunch of really good reasons for the Players to be involved in the Terra Surge aspects of the Anima setting aside from &quot;Most people in the setting like playing this Elder Scrolls-style game.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Originally posted by <b>Planguy</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1470105#post1470105\">View Post</a><br /> My concern is still that the scope of the game seems to be very narrow. Like, you are going to be running a very specific campaign. With Aeon there was definitely a big incentive for players to get involved with various big plotlines, but you didn't necessarily have to. And if you didn't get involved in the various big plots there was still a lot of cool stuff you could do. You could play asteroid miners in some out of the way star system or maybe be private investigators who are being pursued by a powerful Metacorp. Does material from Anima out so far give some ideas of the various adventures you could have that don't involve the larger metaplot? Other than experiences what exactly does playing Terra Surge offer people? Playing a game about someone playing a game is sort of interesting in a meta sense, but is there any actual stakes involved?<br /> <br /> Like my main thought is that Terra Surge involved the use of artificial intelligence in its creation so if the NPC's in the game are actual people then the player's have some more drive to care about everything. Take down that raid boss or a village of real people are going to die! Otherwise it seems like playing the game would be more like playing someone's hobby rather then something meaningful. </div> </div> </div>From what I can tell the setting for this is a single city (Cascade) within a single nation (the FSA). Unlike Adventure, Aberrant or Aeon, you don't have a whole world or possibly multiple worlds (aside from the one in the computer). Within that setting, sure, if you want to play some small-business people or a street gang or whatever, that's fine. However, the plot (not really metaplot) is still going to be happening and some of it will eventually happen to your characters. At that point they can either choose to try to do something about it or just let it keep happening to them.<br /> <br /> So, yes, unlike the other mainline games this is a setting with a small scope and more limited focus. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T15:08:59-08:00","id":1470478,"title":"","content":"That's not surprising. They did say a long time ago, that adventure, aberrant, and Aon will be the tent poles of the trinity continuum, and that other setting are going to be more limited in scope.<br /> <br /> On another front, I haven't been able to keep up with the manuscript. I've had some setbacks IRL that have me working 16-hour days in order to avoid getting buried in a deluge of bills. What interested me about the original notion of anima was the way that it was going to play with the way that technology can blur the line between man and machine, specifically in terms of the human mind and technological abilities to mess with it. Does anima tackle that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T15:50:35-08:00","id":1470484,"title":"","content":"Which is actually a good idea. In the setting secrets, it's plain that what happens in Cascade is a big deal, but equally, sometimes players just want to be local heroes, rather than having universe spanning battles. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T17:06:05-08:00","id":1470488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1470484#post1470484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is actually a good idea. In the setting secrets, it's plain that what happens in Cascade is a big deal, but equally, sometimes players just want to be local heroes, rather than having universe spanning battles.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, it's still a pretty big deal even with a more limited scope/time frame.<br /> <br /> Basically it's the difference between playing Trinity: Ancestry which is a big game set in ancient Greece/Rome/Egypt (like Hercules/Xena) revolving around swords, sandals and something that at least pretends to be sorcery and playing Trinity: Aoowwww That's Hot! which is specifically set in the city of Pompeii around AD 78 or 79.<br /> <br /> Granted that Anima will be focused on one city on a timeline that's months instead of years or decades, but some epic shit is gonna go down in that one city during that time period. Do you want to be part of it or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","user":"johntfs","date":". 12-14-2021, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T21:11:04-08:00","id":1470499,"title":"","content":"So what would you do if you want to play more Anima? Just do different permutations of the same events? Play in a modified setting where Terra Surge is a more long lasting phenomena, getting rid of the metaplot that dictates that the events are going to be at a frenetic pace?<br /> <br /> I did think that the whole concept of Anima reminded me of the Old World of Darkness game Orpheus. A more self-contained experience, very focused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T22:47:14-08:00","id":1470505,"title":"","content":"One thing I like is the discussion as to what Novas can and Cannot do regarding this kind of mind interface. It actually explains why a lot of Nova attempts along those lines were rather &quot;off&quot;, because they were missing the vital noetic connection. Which mind you opens up all kinds of horrific possibilities for attempts at uploading minds that got something... less.<br /> <br /> Of course, now I'm wondering what a mega intelligent nova working with some psions could do. Even if they couldn't directly perceive noetic signatures, they could work with those who could.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T00:53:30-08:00","id":1470512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1470499#post1470499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what would you do if you want to play more Anima? Just do different permutations of the same events? Play in a modified setting where Terra Surge is a more long lasting phenomena, getting rid of the metaplot that dictates that the events are going to be at a frenetic pace?</div> </div> </div> </div>I now slowly creates <b>Trinity Continuum</b> mega-chronicle ( across all/most eras ) - but I plan for now to have <i>Terra Surge</i> one-shot sessions as 'backup plans', when players of my present teams could not meet as a whole. Easier mechanics, MMO environment built and light-hearted take of 'we play only MMO game here, guys!' will probably look great for one-shots. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It also let me test mechanics of <i>T</i><i>erraSurge</i> / MMO-light take on Storypath in those sections. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( I still need to read mechanics chapters of those. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-15-2021, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T03:34:24-08:00","id":1470519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1470505#post1470505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I like is the discussion as to what Novas can and Cannot do regarding this kind of mind interface. It actually explains why a lot of Nova attempts along those lines were rather &quot;off&quot;, because they were missing the vital noetic connection. Which mind you opens up all kinds of horrific possibilities for attempts at uploading minds that got something... less.<br /> <br /> Of course, now I'm wondering what a mega intelligent nova working with some psions could do. Even if they couldn't directly perceive noetic signatures, they could work with those who could.</div> </div> </div> </div>Terra Surge is not a game that can only be played with Glass, the non invasive equipment is used in most of the world and people play everywhere. So, if you place your campaign out of Cascade, it may last until Aeon or even later.<br /> <br /> Cascade and Glass, in the other hand, will end eventually. But if you follow the timeline described, you will have a awesome climax and end of campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T17:52:22-08:00","id":1470567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1470499#post1470499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what would you do if you want to play more Anima? Just do different permutations of the same events? Play in a modified setting where Terra Surge is a more long lasting phenomena, getting rid of the metaplot that dictates that the events are going to be at a frenetic pace?<br /> <br /> I did think that the whole concept of Anima reminded me of the Old World of Darkness game Orpheus. A more self-contained experience, very focused.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. Bear in mind that what we got in the &quot;Spoiler chapters&quot; was a general outline of events as they would occur <i>without PC intervention</i>. PC intervention, AKA players being players exercising their agency in the game can change a bunch of stuff. The action in Anima takes place over a period of weeks and months through 2084-2085 or so. But what happens in those weeks and months is still up to you and your players. If you want to do a full year's worth of play before anything &quot;metaplot-related&quot; happens with your group, that's up to you. Your Anima game can be as short or long as you wish it to be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T02:29:16-08:00","id":1470833,"title":"","content":"Had a discussion about Anima and Glass with a friend. Based on the way it works (A eufiber lattice over and in your brain that is comprised of Nova tech) we had the theory that perhaps a Glass installation would protect someone against a Doyen possession. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca","name":"DarrenDalca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27184_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T10:05:42-08:00","id":1470863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarrenDalca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1470833#post1470833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had a discussion about Anima and Glass with a friend. Based on the way it works (A eufiber lattice over and in your brain that is comprised of Nova tech) we had the theory that perhaps a Glass installation would protect someone against a Doyen possession. Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense to me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T10:31:17-08:00","id":1470865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarrenDalca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1470833#post1470833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had a discussion about Anima and Glass with a friend. Based on the way it works (A eufiber lattice over and in your brain that is comprised of Nova tech) we had the theory that perhaps a Glass installation would protect someone against a Doyen possession. Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the Quantum in Glass strong enough to give people Quantum Flux diseases? Probably not? Then probably not. It'd be like expecting that standing near an X-ray machine or a microwave would protect you from Doyen possession.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T14:21:02-08:00","id":1470882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarrenDalca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1470833#post1470833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had a discussion about Anima and Glass with a friend. Based on the way it works (A eufiber lattice over and in your brain that is comprised of Nova tech) we had the theory that perhaps a Glass installation would protect someone against a Doyen possession. Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>If Glass produced a quantum field strong enough to interfere with psi, people with Glass would presumably set off Aberrant detectors every time they walk by the things, and the FSA never would have approved the technology. There is also the fact that I believe everyone in Cascade is supposed to have Glass by law, and there are apparently several psiads in the city investigating rumors of weird tech, so they'd presumably have Glass implants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T14:39:46-08:00","id":1470886,"title":"","content":"It doesn\u2019t need to be a strong quantum field to block, it can be a tech that just cover brain cells to block it from telepathy, or replace part of the brain with tech.<br /> <br /> On the \u201cby law must have Glass\u201d, I think it\u2019s a bit too much to say you MUST have, it may be very common, but it is said that there are some that don\u2019t have it, and there are the non citizens that are forbidden from having it. If a bunch of Psiads want to be ignored walking in the city they could just pass by as non citizens or just not have glass at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T00:43:10-08:00","id":1470914,"title":"","content":"Gotta remember there is no Psi based detectors in the Anima book. Psion's don't appear till 20 years after Glass is outlawed by the Shanghai Accords. No Psion's or Biotech means that any Aberrant Detectors are either based on Nova-tech and as such not trusted (for the most part) or crude and inexact. We don't have a write up of a Aberrant detector yet but I would image what they are detecting is Quantum Flux rather than just Quantum. If it was that easy to detect Quantum in a human body Dark Star Nova's wouldn't be a thing. However that is just my opinion as there is no official word on it.<br /> <br /> Quantum Flux diseases are caused by Quantum Flux, not just Quantum so equating the power of a thing to whether or not it causes a Quantum Flux diseases doesn't make sense. Aberrant powers cause Quantum Flux disease due to them having a huge amount of Quantum Flux that infects things they use their powers on. Normal Nova Powers have little to no Quantum Flux and as such don't cause any Quantum Flux disease at all, otherwise the colony on Eden would be riddled with Quantum Flux diseases due to the pervasive Nova Power use, and I don't think it's even mentioned.<br /> <br /> Psi and Quantum don't play nice together. As the brain is a fairly delicate organ it would stand to reason that possession is not a brute force attack but rather a delicate processes that uses a small amount of Psi on a very tiny scale to take over a person. Therefore warping a brain in a weak Quantum field could disrupt a Psi based attempt to take it over, due to them interfering with each other.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca","name":"DarrenDalca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27184_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T01:17:30-08:00","id":1470916,"title":"","content":"Well, Telepathy works in an Aberrant (a very powerful Quantum Field), so, there is no reason to believe a weak quantum field would block it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T07:41:15-08:00","id":1470933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarrenDalca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1470914#post1470914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotta remember there is no Psi based detectors in the Anima book. Psion's don't appear till 20 years after Glass is outlawed by the Shanghai Accords. No Psion's or Biotech means that any Aberrant Detectors are either based on Nova-tech and as such not trusted (for the most part) or crude and inexact. We don't have a write up of a Aberrant detector yet but I would image what they are detecting is Quantum Flux rather than just Quantum. If it was that easy to detect Quantum in a human body Dark Star Nova's wouldn't be a thing. However that is just my opinion as there is no official word on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not trusted? The book outright states the FSA was using quantum signature scanners at the Olympic games, and this was treated as a standard procedure that raised no concerns. Aberrant hunters who seek aberrants hiding among the populace are a global phenomenon. Additionally, dark stars have nothing to do with quantum detection. A dark star is any nova whose powers aren't immediately obvious when used in front of an observer. You can have Mega-Intellect 5, Mega-Cunning 5, Mega-Resolve 5, and Mega-Composure 5 and still be a dark star, because there is absolutely nothing about using your powers that looks like someone using powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T11:04:07-08:00","id":1470937,"title":"","content":"Dark Stars aren\u2019t the issue with getting around Quantum Detectors. Dormancy is.<br /> <br /> That and people like Cassel may have made counter-tech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T11:01:37-08:00","id":1471016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1470916#post1470916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Telepathy works in an Aberrant (a very powerful Quantum Field), so, there is no reason to believe a weak quantum field would block it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Glass implants would protect you from Telepathy almost as well as hats made from aluminum foil.<br /> <br /> Honestly at this point I kind of want there to be some kind of resurgence of Glass among anti-psi twits in Aeon based on that concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T13:45:34-08:00","id":1471032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1471016#post1471016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly. Glass implants would protect you from Telepathy almost as well as hats made from aluminum foil.<br /> <br /> Honestly at this point I kind of want there to be some kind of resurgence of Glass among anti-psi twits in Aeon based on that concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Juicy twist. If someone has the potential to be a Psiad or a Nova perhaps using the Glass as a shield might cause a weak awakening of the character's potential. These sparks of power could convince someone they are under noetic attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T23:10:49-08:00","id":1471069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1471032#post1471032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Juicy twist. If someone has the potential to be a Psiad or a Nova perhaps using the Glass as a shield might cause a weak awakening of the character's potential. These sparks of power could convince someone they are under noetic attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thing is that the &quot;current year&quot; in Aeon is 2023, IIRC. Somebody who was 25 in 2084 would be 64 in 2023. So, while they'd be older, there would be plenty of people who remember having/using Glass implants and at least some engineers/designers/ect. who recall how to make them. Shanghai Accords or not, people will find a way. And I could see the FSA maybe reaching back to something that would give them something &quot;kinda-sorta&quot; like Telepathy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T01:24:56-08:00","id":1471073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1471069#post1471069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shanghai Accords or not, people will find a way. And I could see the FSA maybe reaching back to something that would give them something &quot;kinda-sorta&quot; like Telepathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I can easily imagine some people still using illegal Glass implants in 2123. I am just not entirely sure, if the FSA would be among those people. I would suppose, that die FSA, as any good and selfrespecting authoritarian regime, is quite paranoid. Maybe even on a STASI-level. Furthermore, I also would suppose, the higher echelons of the FSA are in the know about the real reasons of the Shanghai Accords. So, in 2123, the FSAs &quot;Powers that be&quot; most certainly know, <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName(