z-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">could be comprimised at any time and at any place.</div></div> </div> </div> For a paranoid secret service, this is pretty much a nightmare scenario. Even if FSA-scientists secretly improved security protocolls of Glass, this would loom above every glass-using operative out there like the sword of Damokles.<br /> <br /> So, I would think, that people who still secretly use Glass are best found among those who are scrupulous and affluent enough to afford a secret Glass-infrastructure, but who don\u00b4t know the full, horrible story of Glass. Certain criminal syndicates perhaps, or deluded cults.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T19:41:52-08:00","id":1471119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Waldi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1471073#post1471073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I can easily imagine some people still using illegal Glass implants in 2123. I am just not entirely sure, if the FSA would be among those people. I would suppose, that die FSA, as any good and selfrespecting authoritarian regime, is quite paranoid. Maybe even on a STASI-level. Furthermore, I also would suppose, the higher echelons of the FSA are in the know about the real reasons of the Shanghai Accords. So, in 2123, the FSAs &amp;quot;Powers that be&amp;quot; most certainly know, <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> that Glass implants are potentially an open gateway for alien spirits or other foreign forces to possess the body of the user</div></div> </div> </div>. Therefore, every operative who uses Glass <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">could be comprimised at any time and at any place.</div></div> </div> </div> For a paranoid secret service, this is pretty much a nightmare scenario. Even if FSA-scientists secretly improved security protocolls of Glass, this would loom above every glass-using operative out there like the sword of Damokles.<br /> <br /> So, I would think, that people who still secretly use Glass are best found among those who are scrupulous and affluent enough to afford a secret Glass-infrastructure, but who don\u00b4t know the full, horrible story of Glass. Certain criminal syndicates perhaps, or deluded cults.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. I wonder if they still use it to play Terra Surge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T20:54:07-08:00","id":1471121,"title":"","content":"I would suppose that die hard fans still use GLASS to play or entertainment - after Shanghai Accords, technology is relative safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T01:08:56-08:00","id":1471129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would suppose that die hard fans still use GLASS to play or entertainment - after Shanghai Accords, technology is relative safe. </div> </div> </div>Is it, or do people use alternative ways of accessing &quot;cyberspace&quot;? I might miss a few details, but as far as I understood the Shanghai Accords, every technology, that connects directly to a users brain (and therefore allows to meddle with said brain) is of limits. Most likely, that does not rule out VR, because you could still access it by VR-Glasses and Body-Suites (which, in the late 21. and early 22. century are likely nowhere as expensive as today.) but a Matrix-like complete immersion seems to be illegal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That makes sense. I wonder if they still use it to play Terra Surge? </div> </div> </div>In my gaming world, they would. The idea is simply too much fun not to use it.<br /> Firstly, having your Posse follow secret shipments of illegal technology and tracking mysterious &quot;ghosts in the optnet&quot; just to find out, that a bunch of REALLY dedicated gamers is behind all this, is awesome. Beeing confronted with someone, who uses illegal stuff for reasons, that are nowhere near evil but just careless because of ignorance could be more interresting than &quot;Those evil Aberrants are at it again! Wack them!&quot;<br /> Secondly, I love the idea of Terra Surge still beeing around in 2123 - in some form or another. In my headspace, it still is a popular fantasy franchise all over the world. It may not be the &quot;new, insanely hot shit&quot; it was during the 2080s, but it is there and, because beeing present for over four decades now, it is more popular than ever. Besides several incarnations of Terra-Surge-Online-Games, several Series of Novels and Comics, Re-Boots and Spin-Offs there are also Action-Figures, Cosplay-Cons and at least three different official Pen-and-Paper-adaptions. In 2123, the Terra-Surge-Fandom more or less works like fandoms of other, long running franchises. There are those typical disputes, about which version of Terra-Surge is the best. There is lots of laughter about badly written &quot;erotic&quot; fanfic. Everybody has fond memories about those awesome animated Terra-Surge-Series from Bohemia, that sadly was cancelled in 2115. And everybody absolutely loathes the goddawfull trilogy of life-action-movies, Asylum made in 2099 on a shoe string budget. (Yes - Asylum still exists in 2123. And they still make horrible movies. Unfortunatly, some evils are here to stay....)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T02:47:47-08:00","id":1471132,"title":"","content":"No matter what is told in Anima or what was told to the public, the entire thing is blamed somehow to the Aberrants and how the control the mind of people that uses computers connected to their brains.<br /> <br /> So, you can say it would be ok for people use Glass after the crisis is solved, but the entire thing is made illegal and a big fear of mind control is created to prevent people from using it. Aberrants are not just the terror of the past, they are the urban legends and the real monsters that people are afraid, telling something would allow an Aberrant to mind control you would be enough to make 95% of the people just give up on using it. Yes, there are a few die hard fans, they would never admit they have one active computer in their minds as it would be illegal, but there are a few people around during Aeon era that still have them.<br /> <br /> Yet, regular VR sets are still available and are not illegal, and Terra Surge is still played after the entire Anima period, as it was before Glass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T02:48:16-08:00","id":1471133,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24955\" data-vbnamecard=\"24955\">Waldi</a> I LOVE your Terra Surge future vision in <b>Aeon</b> era! Totally incorporating it for my games!<br /> <br /> Only I have other idea - <b>HOW casual people play Terra Surge 11 without GLASS?</b> As today, only on VR Glasses and with VR gloves ( like our small, temperature gloves )? <b>Minority Raport </b>like?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PJqbivkm0Ms\" data-code=\"PJqbivkm0Ms\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/PJqbivkm0Ms/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T03:43:10-08:00","id":1471135,"title":"","content":"Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Inputwise, the controlls shown in Minority Report are pretty much, what I would expect from a non-Glass interface for Terra Surge. This, plus some very advanced VR-Headset, that would be as comfy as wearing a beanie. Those, who would like to combine Terra Surge with real life sports would most likely add a virtual treadmill to this configuration. Given the technology level in Aeon, I can imagine some discount treadmills that are only marginaly more expensive than a doormat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T03:48:43-08:00","id":1471136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1471132#post1471132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No matter what is told in Anima or what was told to the public, the entire thing is blamed somehow to the Aberrants and how the control the mind of people that uses computers connected to their brains.<br /> <br /> So, you can say it would be ok for people use Glass after the crisis is solved, but the entire thing is made illegal and a big fear of mind control is created to prevent people from using it. Aberrants are not just the terror of the past, they are the urban legends and the real monsters that people are afraid, telling something would allow an Aberrant to mind control you would be enough to make 95% of the people just give up on using it. Yes, there are a few die hard fans, they would never admit they have one active computer in their minds as it would be illegal, but there are a few people around during Aeon era that still have them.<br /> <br /> Yet, regular VR sets are still available and are not illegal, and Terra Surge is still played after the entire Anima period, as it was before Glass.</div> </div> </div> </div>My main concern here is that if it's a matter of \u201cmind control is bad\u201d, the rise of psions in general, and of telepaths in particular, ought to trigger the same cultural backlash. Explaining why Glass is bad but telepathy is good requires you to walk a very fine line indeed.<br /> <br /> My own dog in this fight, as it were, is that the issue that Glass brings to the fore is identity dissolution: my take on Anima is going to play up how people with Glass gradually stop being who they were as the memory transplants that the Glass enables slowly corrodes the person's sense of self. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This is in contrast to Anima's official explanation of what went wrong, where everything gets blamed on an alien invasion enabled by Aberrant technology, rather than the inherent danger of a technology that focuses on treating human minds like digital archives. You get the impression that if there was no Ascendancy, Glass would have been perfectly fine.</div></div> </div> </div> As is, I'm almost inclined to introduce something vaguely like Vampire's Humanity trait for Glass users as a way of measuring how much of a toll the technology has taken on a given person's, well, personhood. Almost. CtL2e's Clarity might be a better game system to poach, as it's closer to the notion that Glass damages the mind and makes it harder to distinguish reality from fantasy. One common consequence of too much Glass use, for example, might be that the character identifies more with his Anima than with his \u201creal-world\u201d persona, to the point that he starts thinking of his time in Cascade as the Anima visiting another world, rather than Terra Surge being a fictional world that a Cascadian visits. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This still ties in with the secret alien invasion thing, in that at least some of these cases where the Anima has become dominant would in fact be alien minds possessing human hosts; the difference is that that becomes almost incidental rather than being at the core of what's going on.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That, to me, is the real heart of Anima.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T04:07:39-08:00","id":1471137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1471136#post1471136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main concern here is that if it's a matter of \u201cmind control is bad\u201d, the rise of psions in general, and of telepaths in particular, ought to trigger the same cultural backlash. Explaining why Glass is bad but telepathy is good requires you to walk a very fine line indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a very good point indeed! And one, that can easily become an awesome storyhook if brougt up ingame. It is quite easy to fall into a black-and-white-pattern, where Psions are good, while those who fear Psions are just some deluded Ignoramuses (just as your Trump-voting Uncle from the US) or just plain evil hatemongers. But the potential situation here is much more interessting than that. Those, who fear that Telepathy could potentially be just as dangerous as Glass was, DO HAVE A POINT. Of course, most PC-Telepaths are very likely to be good guys. But maybe, others are not? As a mere Baseline, you can never be sure - and you cant defend yourself. How do you deal with people, who fear you and your powers not because they are some spitefull Rednecks but because they have legitimate concerns?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T04:14:42-08:00","id":1471138,"title":"","content":"The general public after anima don\u2019t think it\u2019s ok to have computers in their brain because of Aberrants, that is what was probably the explanation FSA government gave, and the explanation for he accord in 2086. I am not questioning real reasons or why I would not let them to have their Glasses still active, I am just point what the general public would think about it.<br /> <br /> To be fair, my post was responding to the following post:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1471121#post1471121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would suppose that die hard fans still use GLASS to play or entertainment - after Shanghai Accords, technology is relative safe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, on Psi is ok and Aberrants are evil, I agree with you completely. The way you are describing results in a much more solid explanation why messing with memories using Glass is bad and Psions are not.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Coalition were once, or at least the masters of Coalition were, a highly developed Psi race that gave up on their psi powers because they were losing individuality. In other words, Psi is as dangerous to the individuality as Glass is, in the long run. Sure, you need to develop Society to a certain point before Psi gets the entire society into a single hivemind, but it\u2019s still possible, and people were afraid of it enough to cut their psionic potential from their DNA at least once.<br /> <br /> I think the entire point of Aeon era is this duality of Evil and Good that are basically the same but with different titles to make they look the way they do. In the end Aberrants are not that bad, and Psions are not that good either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 12-23-2021, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T18:04:56-08:00","id":1471168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Waldi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1471129#post1471129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it, or do people use alternative ways of accessing &amp;quot;cyberspace&amp;quot;? I might miss a few details, but as far as I understood the Shanghai Accords, every technology, that connects directly to a users brain (and therefore allows to meddle with said brain) is of limits. Most likely, that does not rule out VR, because you could still access it by VR-Glasses and Body-Suites (which, in the late 21. and early 22. century are likely nowhere as expensive as today.) but a Matrix-like complete immersion seems to be illegal.<br /> <br /> <br /> In my gaming world, they would. The idea is simply too much fun not to use it.<br /> Firstly, having your Posse follow secret shipments of illegal technology and tracking mysterious &amp;quot;ghosts in the optnet&amp;quot; just to find out, that a bunch of REALLY dedicated gamers is behind all this, is awesome. Beeing confronted with someone, who uses illegal stuff for reasons, that are nowhere near evil but just careless because of ignorance could be more interresting than &amp;quot;Those evil Aberrants are at it again! Wack them!&amp;quot;<br /> Secondly, I love the idea of Terra Surge still beeing around in 2123 - in some form or another. In my headspace, it still is a popular fantasy franchise all over the world. It may not be the &amp;quot;new, insanely hot shit&amp;quot; it was during the 2080s, but it is there and, because beeing present for over four decades now, it is more popular than ever. Besides several incarnations of Terra-Surge-Online-Games, several Series of Novels and Comics, Re-Boots and Spin-Offs there are also Action-Figures, Cosplay-Cons and at least three different official Pen-and-Paper-adaptions. In 2123, the Terra-Surge-Fandom more or less works like fandoms of other, long running franchises. There are those typical disputes, about which version of Terra-Surge is the best. There is lots of laughter about badly written &amp;quot;erotic&amp;quot; fanfic. Everybody has fond memories about those awesome animated Terra-Surge-Series from Bohemia, that sadly was cancelled in 2115. And everybody absolutely loathes the goddawfull trilogy of life-action-movies, Asylum made in 2099 on a shoe string budget. (Yes - Asylum still exists in 2123. And they still make horrible movies. Unfortunatly, some evils are here to stay....)</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like your interpretation of Terra Surge in the age of Aeon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T18:49:47-08:00","id":1471169,"title":"","content":"<b><i>Shanghai Accords</i> are global law, when passed? </b>Cause <b>Anima</b> is written like it surely is in forced in FSA - but not so much like in European Union, China Protectorate, Sudam\u00e9rica or United African Nations. Or it is as I read the text of era. ( I may read it wrong. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-23-2021, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T19:16:47-08:00","id":1471171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1465651-trinity-continuum-anima-previews?p=1471169#post1471169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>Shanghai Accords</i> are global law, when passed? </b>Cause <b>Anima</b> is written like it surely is in forced in FSA - but not so much like in European Union, China Protectorate, Sudam\u00e9rica or United African Nations. Or it is as I read the text of era. ( I may read it wrong. )</div> </div> </div> </div>the Shanghai Accords haven\u2019t happened yet in Anima.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T20:42:05-08:00","id":1471175,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">2086 \u2014 After several serious incidents, the <br /> UN passes the Shanghai Accords. This treaty <br /> bans computer enhancement and other tech-<br /> nology that allows electronic access to thoughts <br /> and memories except under special license. The <br /> Shanghai Accords also prohibit all but the most <br /> carefully controlled and monitored uses of AS <br /> (artificial sentience). This ruling has no effect <br /> on Nippon, but elsewhere, public opinion turns <br /> against cyberware and hardtech in general.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2014TC:\u00c6on</b> p.26</div><br /> And <b>TC:Anima</b> is set in 2084, two years before the Accords go into effect. Basically, it's the \u201cseveral serious incidents\u201d that are referenced in the above timeline entry, either in part or in whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-24T17:52:33-08:00","id":1471219,"title":"","content":"I wonder if anyone is still looking at Glass in the Trinity era? I mean, it's funny, but being that Glass is Nova tech, it might actually make life more difficult for the Doyen, say by having &quot;error checking&quot; routines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-24T20:24:32-08:00","id":1471226,"title":"","content":"It require special permission, as per the Shanghai Accords, but it would be possible.<br /> Or just being a criminal with an illicit and hidden implant.<br /> Both require ST permission, just as any game warping backstory. Like playing a member of the Mercer family. Allowed only with permission is how I handle with playing against type. Others include playing a Nova in the \u00c6on or Anima eras, playing a Stalwart member of the Coalition, playing an Alien in an Aberrant game, ties to major NPCs or secret groups in the gameworld.<br /> <br /> So yes, certain characters might have access to Glass or equivalent tech in \u00c6on but that is utterly dependant on the ST and would either require strict supervision in game (because of the Accords) or keeping it a secret piece of incredibly illegal cyberware, likely from Nippon if not a criminal organisation or Shadow Society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 12-25-2021, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}